From: tcdent <tcdent@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 17:47:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 11/38] rust: sync: add Locked, proof that an embedded lock is
 held

Some kernel objects carry their own lock, for example an inode's rw
semaphore or a folio's lock bit. Locked<T, Marker> wraps a reference to
such an object as evidence that the lock is held, so an API can require
the lock at the type level. The VFS hands callbacks objects it has
already locked and will unlock itself; those wrap the guard in
ManuallyDrop.

Lifted from Wedson Almeida Filho's "Rust abstractions for VFS" RFC v2
(May 2024), where it lived in kernel::types.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SKmspe5nVbuvzdvYZa9UhW
